  "description": "XOSZIQ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C78 H80 N22 O32 Tb7 3+,3(N1 O3 1-),9(C2 H3 N1),2(C1 H4 O1),3(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 4 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 4 O neighbors; Tb5 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb6 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb7 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.507-3.895 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.81-110.60°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Tb7(L)6(μ3-OH)8(NO3)4]·(NO3)3·9CH3CN·2CH3OH·3H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 3 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
